# E0029: the dangling else. A `then` body is a primary-expression, which
# excludes `if` and `match` -- exactly the two forms that consume an `else`.
# Written bare, the `else` below has two candidate owners and binds silently to
# the inner `if`. Braces say which was meant: `then { if .. else .. }` gives the
# inner one, `then { if .. } else ..` the outer.
main: function is {
    a: 0
    b: 5
    if b > 3 then if b > 99 then a = 1 else a = 2
    print "a=\{a}"
}
